  "headline": "Flash Floods Hit Multiple Regions Across Indonesia Impacting Thousands",
  "seoTitle": "Flash Floods Damage Gayo Lues Aceh and Other Regions",
  "metaDescription": "Persistent flooding across Indonesia has impacted thousands of residents in Aceh, Bengkulu, and Banten, leading to search and recovery efforts.",
  "aiSummaryBullets": [
    "Severe flooding continues to affect thousands of residents in Bengkulu and Mataram following heavy rainfall.",
    "Regional authorities report thousands of households impacted across multiple provinces including Aceh and West Kalimantan.",
    "Government agencies are distributing aid and working to restore damaged infrastructure and transit routes."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "Indonesia is currently experiencing widespread flooding across several provinces, triggered by prolonged heavy rainfall. In Aceh, the impact has been extensive, affecting over 21,000 residents and damaging local infrastructure, prompting ongoing government aid distribution and recovery efforts. Recent reports indicate that 2,539 households in Bengkulu and 373 households in Mataram have been affected, though many residents in the latter remain in their homes. Additionally, flash floods were reported in West Kalimantan's Melawi region and near a popular waterfall in Bogor, where a woman was reported missing. While some recovery work has been successful, such as the restoration of the Takengon-Gayo Lues road access, regional disaster management agencies continue to monitor the situation closely as thousands of families face the consequences of rising water levels in submerged villages.",
